## 6. Standards and plan anchors

| Source | Sections/lines | Constraint relevant here |
|---|---|---|
| `docs/dnssec-expansion/inputs/worker-plan.html` | `:1110-1126` (`DNS22 — Private DNS, local anchors and conditional forwarding`) | Two views, named trust stores/routes/fixture identities; forwarding is not delegation/anchor bootstrap; public root does not trust unrelated private hierarchy; do not merge caches/keys; no RFC-mandated split-DNS product design |
| Source map `docs/dnssec-expansion/source-groups.json` | `S01` RFC4033; `S04` RFC9499; `S14` RFC5011/RFC9718; `S23` RFC5625/RFC3225 | Plan’s DNS22 source groups |
| `sources/resolution/s01-rfc4033-text.txt` | `:288-301` (Trust Anchor); `:383-434` (§3.1 auth chain/local policy); `:492-569` (§5 states/scope); `:606-655` (§7 stub AD/CD) | Anchor configured in the validating resolver; local policy may configure non-root anchors; states depend on the configured anchor; stub AD is a hint, not local validation |
| `sources/resolution/s04-rfc9499-text.txt` | `:932-941` (Forwarder); `:975-983` (View); `:1525-1556` (Validation); `:1652-1684` (§11 states) | Views/forwarders are local deployment concepts; DNSSEC states are per validating resolver/anchor |
| `sources/resolution/s06-rfc4035-text.txt` | `:882-892` (§3.1.6 authoritative CD clear); `:917-1020` (§3.2 recursive DO/CD/AD); `:1420-1434` (§5.1 islands); `:1435-1465` (§5.2 referrals) | Authoritative response clears CD; recursive server copies CD; AD only when all answer/authority RRsets are authentic; island security needs a separately obtained anchor; DS authenticates child DNSKEY |
| `sources/resolution/s03-rfc6840-text.txt` | `:511-531` (§5.7-5.8 AD in query/reply); `:533-555` (§5.9 CD on upstream queries) | `AD=1` in the stub query signals understanding/interest; resolver may set AD when DO/AD requested and data authentic; CD=1 upstream is the selected validation model |
| `sources/resolution/s23-rfc5625-text.txt` | `:125-178` (§3 transparency); `:179-220` (§4 conformance) | A forwarder is transparent about flags/data and is not itself an authenticated delegation or anchor bootstrap |
| `sources/resolution/s22-rfc1035-text.txt` | `:1401-1571` (§4.1.1-4.1.3); `:2544-2548` (ID/question correlation) | Exact header flags, QDCOUNT, question identity, and message-ID/question correlation |
| `numeric/sources/rfc5011.txt` | `:104-140`, `:597-632` (§8.1) | Zone owner creates/distributes keys; resolver owner decides acceptance; manual/out-of-band trust-anchor updates are outside RFC5011; do not conflate key identity with acceptance |

The plan’s S14 reference is context for managed/root anchors; this case intentionally uses static out-of-band/operator provisioning, not RFC5011 automated update. No RFC5011 state-machine behavior is selected here.

